  "ai.orion81Completely": "<0>Orion-81 is a completely AI-generated project.<\/0> Every line of Orion-81's own code was written with Claude Code, directed by the founder. Every ship, map, texture and sound was generated by tools that Claude Code wrote. The founder decides what to build; Claude Code works out how. The open-source libraries it builds on are listed below under 'Not AI-made'. One item is still open and is shown openly: a <1>licence review<\/1> of game code that came across from the GPL prototype.",
  "ai.orionBegan28": "Orion began on 28 September 2026 as a prototype on the open-source Quake III Arena engine (GPL), with ships from Elite Dangerous as its inspiration. On day two the game's code moved onto BuB, a new engine written with Claude Code; the game modules came across from the prototype and were renamed. Release 0.3.0 gave all 16 ship classes new hulls of their own. A licence-compliance review is checking whether any of the code is still derived from the GPL original, and whether the early ship designs are too close to their inspiration. An automated similarity scan of the code against the GPL prototype's source ran on 8 October 2026, and the expert review of its matches is in progress. Anything that is derived will be rewritten or redesigned.",
