  "d.109szp9": "Solid terrain or structures to collide with.",
  "d.10azxrl": "Three solar radii above the photosphere. Shade is life: the platform's shield, the comet, the big hulls. Flares come every few minutes.",
  "d.10wlatv": "A custom colour whose brightest channel is below 0x40 reads as STOCK, so a shield never goes invisible.",
  "d.11cuwtu": "ROCKETS",
  "d.11jyj1n": "A destroyer built around a medium spinal railgun, with laser turrets and sixteen rocket cells.",
  "d.11phsqq": "A game publisher that allows 100% AI-generated content publishes the game.",
  "d.11zjijr": "Weapons can be deployed and retracted (retracted weapons are hidden), and ships no longer trail smoke.",
  "d.11zq7hg": "The look: physically lit cockpits, classed stars, a ringed gas giant, a galaxy and nebula backdrop, engine plumes and navigation lights; the 0.1.0 play feel locked.",
  "d.12zyt91": "ANVIL, the hangar image from the game menu (hull as built for 0.3.0 and later; native size 256 x 128). In-game capture, version 0.6.1",
  "d.13cb0px": "Hostiles over the city, with engine plumes (GLASGOW). In-game capture, version 0.5.3",
  "d.1436q76": "Version 0.5.1 frozen: hardpoint seats, six-rocket volleys, and an ANVIL bay that launches 10 NEEDLEs.",
  "d.14s5uo6": "Engine plumes on a capital ship and a fighter. In-game capture, version 0.5.3",
  "d.14vqvyw": "The ANVIL with its hangar bay open. In-game capture, version 0.6.1",
  "d.14zbb1f": "A small fighter under fire from a hostile wing in the THETA-7 asteroid field, its shield bubble glowing.",
  "d.15oh132": "versions frozen",
  "d.16dme8w": "Fixed lasers converge on one aim point in front of the ship.",
  "d.16sui9e": "City-sized flagship with a rotating habitat drum, two heavy spinal rails and a forest of guns.",
  "d.177y6xj": "Double boost.",
  "d.178olkv": "The ANVIL destroyer with its hangar bay door open and light spilling out.",
  "d.17hv0ld": "No gravity: free fall.",
  "d.18fr12s": "INTERCEPTOR",
  "d.18l8y3y": "Built so far by one founder.",
  "d.18qbnrf": "AI-generated trailer is produced along with AI-generated artwork.",
  "d.18qvzf2": "NEEDLE, the hangar image from the game menu (hull as built for 0.3.0 and later; native size 256 x 128). In-game capture, version 0.6.1",
  "d.18yyc5": "Modules take damage separately and the hull breaks apart.",
  "d.194nnt6": "A long-legged survey craft with foil-wrapped tanks, a sensor mast and the biggest boost reserve.",
  "d.198svbo": "Version 0.5.0 frozen: physically lit cockpits, classed stars, a ringed gas giant and a nebula backdrop.",
  "d.19i63zk": "The ORION-1 as shown in the game's hangar menu, version 0.6.1 hull, three-quarter view on black.",
  "d.19mf6u": "MERIDIAN, the hangar image from the game menu (hull as built for 0.3.0 and later; native size 256 x 128). In-game capture, version 0.6.1",
  "d.19up4m2": "DEBRIS",
  "d.1adjth7": "An armoured cruiser: thick belts, twin rail turrets, a spinal rail and heavy torpedoes.",
  "d.1bhctvm": "THE MOON (COPERNICUS): ridged lunar terrain with craters under a black sky.",
  "d.1bk3qbs": "Box arena 24 km by 24 km, soft ceiling 9 km.",
  "d.1bkjp1s": "Version 0.2.3 frozen: deployable and retractable weapons.",
  "d.1bt06ve": "Spinal railgun: hold to charge, release to fire.",
  "d.1c3ocas": "FREE FALL",
  "d.1c7mz24": "Box arena 16 km by 12 km, soft ceiling 2.7 km.",
  "d.1c9et86": "Version 0.5.2 frozen: squadron stances, a ROCKETS INCOMING sign and turret seats.",
  "d.1czllhs": "CRUISER",
  "d.1dlvg7e": "LIGHT FIGHTER",
  "d.1dlyq4f": "420 km above the night side, three minutes before orbital sunrise. Ashgrove Station, the debris of an old break-up, and Europe's lights sliding by below.",
  "d.1dmfq0q": "Linked into the game by the toolchain",
  "d.1e2mh2n": "Moving to Unreal Engine 5 is a rewrite.",
  "d.1e63f23": "Air drag applies.",
  "d.1ea9win": "A battlecruiser that trades armour for a huge drive section and two heavy spinal rails.",
  "d.1eoopdx": "Lock-on rockets: a rocket is guided only if its lock is complete when it launches.",
  "d.1eytq94": "Release 0.3.0 gives all 16 ship classes new hulls (visual only: names, roles, stats and hardpoint layouts carry over).",
  "d.1f5e5lj": "CARRIER",
  "d.1fslkx6": "The ANVIL launches ten allied NEEDLEs from its hangar bay.",
  "d.1ggqqf2": "BATTLECRUISER",
  "d.1gjlmo6": "THETA-7 ASTEROID FIELD: a sparse field of rocks lit by a distant sun.",
  "d.1gppke0": "A shielded fighter with other ships trailing engine plumes in the THETA-7 field.",
  "d.1gzjma": "VACUUM",
  "d.1gzr9mh": "The BASTION as shown in the game's hangar menu, version 0.6.1 hull, three-quarter view on black.",
  "d.1h04cn8": "A photoreal look: image-based lighting, ambient occlusion, soft sun shadows and a filmic grade, with a REALISM menu toggle, and polished BASTION and IRONCLAD hulls.",
  "d.1h4mkmg": "Blender is used to produce the models and animations.",
  "d.1hbx1mh": "Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception; mingw-w64 permissive / public domain",
  "d.1hg3yte": "GRAVITY 1/6 G",
  "d.1hgnwl0": "240 M, SEE-THROUGH HANGAR",
  "d.1hhlmv3": "Volleys of six rockets.",
  "d.1hi6fk9": "HALBERD, the hangar image from the game menu (hull as built for 0.3.0 and later; native size 256 x 128). In-game capture, version 0.6.1",
  "d.1hiyfm4": "Drifting asteroids.",
  "d.1hrnfcm": "The RAMPART as shown in the game's hangar menu, version 0.6.1 hull, three-quarter view on black.",
  "d.1hwe7q8": "Version 0.2.2 frozen: a free-view camera and an AUTO mode that attacks the nearest hostile.",
  "d.1i6l74z": "A low pass over the terraced east wall of Copernicus at the sunset terminator, Earth high overhead. One-sixth gravity and no air: every arc is ballistic.",
  "d.1ib4qda": "Some carry fixed rotary miniguns beside the lasers.",
  "d.1iglk9h": "PERIHELION, 4 SOLAR RADII: the Sun's disc with sunspots and a prominence.",
  "d.1imx84h": "LOW EARTH ORBIT: a ring station with solar panels above the curve of the Earth.",
  "d.1iuw2c3": "A free-view orbit camera, an AUTO mode that attacks the nearest hostile, a switch between AUTO and holding course, and a smooth hand-back to the pilot.",
  "d.1j7mgjz": "Hostile AI ANVILs launch their wings in battle, carrier craft return to dock, craft wear their carrier's shield colour, and railguns zoom in automatically.",
  "d.1kbbopx": "Web fonts on this website",
  "d.1lkmy5i": "maps",
  "d.1lnbgnt": "BULK FREIGHTER",
  "d.1lqtgss": "FLARES",
  "d.1lu6hys": "LAN co-op waves",
  "d.1m02vrd": "The LOADOUT screen for the ORION-1. In-game capture, version 0.6.0",
  "d.1m7j4wn": "The economy and online multiplayer are not built, and how paid ships stay fair in player-versus-player is still being designed.",
  "d.1mqb5qu": "The first round of developers and graphic designers who lost their jobs to AI are hired with the Kickstarter money.",
  "d.1ncvhzy": "A laser beam in flight. In-game capture, version 0.5.0",
  "d.1nnq5c9": "tracker items, EP-001 to EP-021: game, tooling, policy and audit work",
  "d.1o102o0": "THRESHER, the hangar image from the game menu (hull as built for 0.3.0 and later; native size 256 x 128). In-game capture, version 0.6.1",
  "d.1o89nc1": "The ANVIL with its bay open, a still for the fighting styles viewer.",
  "d.1ou7t1x": "ATMOSPHERE",
  "d.1pfk73q": "Armour first, questions later. Two laser pairs, two light guns and twelve light rockets, four of them self-guided.",
  "d.1pg1xjs": "HAULER",
  "d.1pptvj": "BASTION, the hangar image from the game menu (hull as built for 0.3.0 and later; native size 256 x 128). In-game capture, version 0.6.1",
  "d.1q40xi9": "LEVIATHAN, the hangar image from the game menu (hull as built for 0.3.0 and later; native size 256 x 128). In-game capture, version 0.6.1",
  "d.1qabcqp": "A grounded, hard-science-fiction look, half-speed mechanics, rockets and railguns, 16 ships from 12 m to 1.2 km, and the Glasgow map.",
