  "faq.freePlay": "Is it free to play?",
  "faq.n07Questions": "07 · Questions",
  "faq.notYetLan": "Not yet. LAN multiplayer on the same network works today (since 0.2.0); online play is not built.",
  "faq.prototypeWasBuilt": "The prototype was built on the open-source Quake III Arena engine (GPL) and took Elite Dangerous ships as inspiration. On day two the game's code moved onto BuB, a new engine written with Claude Code; the game modules came across from the prototype and were renamed. Release 0.3.0 gave all 16 ship classes new hulls. A licence-compliance review is checking whether any of the code is still derived from the GPL original and whether the early ship designs are too close to their inspiration. An automated similarity scan of the code against the GPL prototype's source ran on <0/>, and the expert review of its matches is in progress. Anything that is derived will be rewritten or redesigned. Until the review is finished, we do not claim the answer is no.",
  "faq.questions": "Questions",
  "faq.shipsArtInterface": "Ships, art, interface and more, as revenue allows. <0>The ledger on this page<\/0> lists every element and will show each replacement and its designer.",
  "faq.shipsUpgradesPlanned": "Ships and upgrades are planned to be earnable by playing or buyable. How paid ships stay fair in player-versus-player is still being designed.",
  "faq.thatPlanFree": "That is the plan: free to play with optional in-game currency and cosmetics. It is not built yet.",
  "faq.wasAnyoneS": "Was anyone's work copied?",
  "faq.whenOutWhat": "When is it out, and on what?",
  "faq.whichPartsWill": "Which parts will people replace, and how will I know?",
  "faq.whyWouldAi": "Why would an AI-made game help designers?",
  "faq.willPayWin": "Will it be pay to win?",
  "faq.windowsPcThere": "Windows PC. There is no release date and no price yet.",
